"A body mended by a healer can suddenly revert, which is incredibly rare."
"A healed bone may break again a week later as the Healer's work undoes itself."
"Reversion is commoner after intensive or repeated healing and with Avowed Healers."
"Wizard healing is gentler and more customized; non-Avowed bodies are more delicate."
"Reversions usually come from a confluence of fragilities, complications or accidents."
"Healing commands reality to reassemble, and like any spell it can meet resistance."
"Damage can become embroidered onto the self, so removing it may harm more than leaving it."
